## 🎨 UI / WIDGET RULES

### Widget Structure
- Prefer `StatelessWidget`. Use `ConsumerWidget` only when reading providers.
- Split large widgets immediately — max ~80 lines per widget build method.
- Const constructors everywhere possible.

```dart
// CORRECT
class ProductCard extends StatelessWidget {
  const ProductCard({super.key, required this.product});
  final Product product;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Card(
    child: ListTile(
      title: Text(product.name),
      subtitle: Text('₹${product.price}'),
    ),
  );
}
```

### Theme
- NEVER use hardcoded colors (`Colors.blue`, `Color(0xFF...)`) in widgets.
- Always use `Theme.of(context).colorScheme.*` or defined `AppColors` constants.
- Use `TextTheme` from context for all text styles.

```dart
// CORRECT
Text(title, style: Theme.of(context).textTheme.titleLarge)
Container(color: Theme.of(context).colorScheme.surface)

// WRONG
Text(title, style: const TextStyle(fontSize: 18, color: Colors.black))
```

### Navigation
- Use `GoRouter` (preferred) or `auto_route`. Never use raw `Navigator.push`.
- Define all routes in `core/router/app_router.dart`.

### Loading & Error States
Every async UI must handle all 3 states:
- Loading → `AppLoader()` (custom shimmer or spinner)
- Error → `ErrorView(message, onRetry)` 
- Data → actual content widget

