## 🧹 CODE STYLE

- Dart 3 features: use `switch` expressions, records, patterns where appropriate.
- All public APIs must have dartdoc comments (`///`).
- No `dynamic` or `Object?` unless absolutely necessary — always type explicitly.
- Line length: 100 characters max.
- Run `dart fix --apply` and `dart format .` mentally before suggesting code.
- Prefer `final` over `var`; prefer `const` constructors.
- Avoid deep widget nesting — extract into named widgets immediately.

```dart
// CORRECT — Dart 3 pattern matching
final label = switch (status) {
  OrderStatus.pending   => 'Pending',
  OrderStatus.confirmed => 'Confirmed',
  OrderStatus.delivered => 'Delivered',
};

// CORRECT — Records
(String name, double price) getProductSummary(Product p) =>
    (p.name, p.price);
```

